# Verify by looking

Any change to `engine3/`, a shader, a groom, a rig, or `engine/` must end with rendering a contact sheet and inspecting it.

Never report an art change as done on the basis of code reading or a passing unit test. The agent cannot see; the harness is its eyes.

- 3D: `node tools/shot3d.js` (and `--sheet <name>` once named sheets exist). Attach the PNG. Look at it.
- 2D (until swapped): `node tools/sheet.js`.
- After a render-path change, also run `node tools/perf3d.js`.
- If the 64px greyscale silhouette does not make the species unmistakable, the geometry is wrong. Say so. Do not tune a shader around it.
